{
  "about": [
    "Every study-record field the site reads, as paths into one record of data/demographics.partN.json.gz.",
    "A path is a key ('status'), a key inside an object ('race.reported'), or a key on every item of a list ('study_sites[].country'). The contract asks that the key be present; its value may be null or empty, which is how a record says 'none'.",
    "Classes say what reads the field. core: the dashboard, its filters and share links, over every record at load. studies_tab: the Studies table, its tooltips and the publications and breakdown views. detail: the study and geography-breakdown pop-ups only.",
    "Today the part files carry all three classes. A later change may move studies_tab and detail fields out of the parts into files fetched when needed; core stays in the parts.",
    "The engine's weekly publish reads this file (and data_budget.json) and refuses to push parts that drop a listed field. tests/study_record_contract.test.mjs keeps it honest against app.js and checks the published parts against it."
  ],
